<figcaption>Published evals cover three types and part of two more; the two open types sit at opposite ends of the Dutch-book scale: constraint consistency, which a book prices exactly, and method consistency, which it prices only as a metaphor. In each glyph, solid marks are the model’s answers, grey marks are what consistency requires, and the bracketed number is the size of the violation (the shaded tail is belief the bound rules out). Repeatability, contextual and method values are illustrative; the others are computed from the page’s example or stated inputs.</figcaption>
